                <pb facs="0177" n="73" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg73"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mizner to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San
                                Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-08-12"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 12, 1890</date>.
                        (Received August 12.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Mizner informs Mr. Blaine that peace has been suggested by the Provisional
                    Government of Salvador upon terms of nonintervention, and that he will telegraph
                    from Guatemala on the 16th instant, as soon as he can confer with the Guatemalan
                    Government. He reports that armies are quiet and in camp.</p>
            </div>
